VAASA.INF Finland, Vaasa, U of Vaasa, Timo Salmi
Updated Wed 5-August-1992

FINLAND
Location:         Northern Europe, Scandinavia
Independence:     since 1917
Economic system:  free market economy
Political System: western democracy, multiparty system
Population:       5 milj.
Area:             338 000 sq. km (Great Britain 244 000,
                  Germany 357 335, Italy 301 000 sq. km)
Lakes:            187 888
Islands:          179 584
Common borders with: Sweden    586 km (264 miles)
                     Norway    716 km (445 miles)
                     Russia  1 269 km (788 miles)
Main Industries:  Metal and engineering industry  38 %
                  Forest industry                 19 %
                  Chemical industry               11 %
                  Food industry                   11 %
                  Textile industry                 6 %
                  Other                           15 %

Time zone: UTC+2 in winter, UTC+3 during summer daylight saving time


VAASA
Location: on the western coast of Finland, 400 km (250 miles)
          northwest of Helsinki
Founded:  in 1606
Population: 54271, of which about 3/4 Finnish-speaking and
            1/4 Swedish-speaking
Area: 397 sq. km of which 258 is maritime
Climate: The annual mean temperature + 5.1 C, warmest in July,
         average 15.2 C and coldest in January, average - 6.7 C.
         Windy and sunny in Finnish comparison because of
         the western coastal location.
Employed persons by type of economic activity:
   Public services    40.4 %
   Industry           28.6 %
   Private services   22.3 %
   Constructions       6.2 %
   Primary production  1.3 %


UNIVERSITY OF VAASA (1-Jan-1992)
Founded: in 1968
Total graduate student enrollment:         2312
 in economics and business administration: 1488
Post graduate student enrollment:
 - Economics and business administration    100
 - The humanities                            45
 - The social sciences                       19
Personnel: teaching personnel 136
           other personnel    154

Faculties, Disciplines and Affiliated Institutions:

1) Faculty of Business Administration is divided into five
departments:
- Department of Management and Organization
- Department of Marketing (subjects: marketing and international
  marketing)
- Department of Economics
- Department of Law (commerce, and corporate taxation)
- Department of Economic Geography.
Degrees granted: Master, Licentiate, and Doctorate of Economics and
Business Management

2) Faculty of Accounting and Industrial Management:
- Department of Accounting and Business Finance
- Department of Mathematics and Statistics (operations research and
  management science)
- Department of Information Technology and Production Management
  (including physics as a minor subject)
Degrees granted: Master, Licentiate, and Doctorate of Economics and
Business Management

3) Faculty of Humanities:
- Department of English
- Department of Scandinavian Languages
- Department of German
- Department of Finnish
- Department of Communication Studies (applied linguistics, in
  formation science)
Degrees granted: Master, Licentiate, and Doctorate of Arts

4) Faculty of Social Sciences, which is not divided into
   departments. The disciplines are
- public Administration
- public Law
- social Health
- economic Sociology
Degrees granted: Master, Licentiate, and Doctorate of Administrative
Sciences.

Affiliated Institutions are Library, Computer Centre, Centre for
Continuing Education and Western-Finland Centre for Economic
Research.


